{
  "id" : "yhqp-riqs",
  "name" : "Street Sweeping Schedule",
  "assetType" : "dataset",
  "attribution" : "San Francisco Public Works",
  "attributionLink" : "http://www.sfdpw.org",
  "averageRating" : 0,
  "category" : "City Infrastructure",
  "createdAt" : 1578422960,
  "description" : "<strong>A. SUMMARY</strong>\nMechanical street sweeping and street cleaning schedule managed by San Francisco Public Works.\n\n<strong>B. HOW THE DATASET IS CREATED</strong>\nThis dataset is created by extracting all street sweeping schedule data from a Department of Public Works database, it is then geocoded to add common identifiers such as Centerline Network Number (\"CNN\") then published to the open data portal.\n\n<strong>C. UPDATE PROCESS</strong>\nThis dataset will be updated on an 'as needed' basis, when sweeping schedules change.\n\n<strong>D. HOW TO USE THIS DATASET</strong>\nUse this dataset to understand, track, or analyze street sweeping in San Francisco.\n\n<strong>Please note that bike lane sweeping is not included in this dataset.</strong>\nPublic Works maintains a route book for bike lane sweeping, but the schedule is not as specific as regular street sweeping.  Sweeping may occur any day of the week during the following timeframes:\n(1) 6:00 p.m. to 1:00 a.m.\n(2) 12:00 a.m. to 7:00 a.m.\n\nActual service may vary depending on staffing, equipment availability, and operational needs.",
